GoldLink's change to melonDS (UC9 §4): a wider picture.

- GPU3D: with WideSide > 0 and a full-screen viewport, vertices and box tests have their
  clip-space x scaled by 256 / (256 + 2 * WideSide) before clipping, and the viewport maps them
  onto 256 + 2 * WideSide pixels: the 3D view keeps more of the scene on each side, and the
  middle 256 pixels are as before. Position tests are left alone (the game reads them back).
- GPU3D_Soft: the buffers are MaxWideSide (64) wider on each side; GetLine still gives the
  screen's 256 pixels to the 2D engine; GetWideLine gives the whole line.
- GPU2D_Soft: each regular-display line also gets its side strips, composed by running the line
  again with every horizontal position shifted by 256 (text scroll, affine references, sprites'
  x, the wide 3D line); windows count as outside; 256-wide text maps are left out (they would
  repeat themselves); master brightness applies. Everything a pass changes is put back.

Applied by build.rs to a copy of the submodule (which stays at upstream).

